# Extended regular expressions matched against the destination host.
# Anchored on purpose: `^api\.openai\.com$` must not also match
# `api.openai.com.attacker.tld`.

# ── inference providers actually connected on this instance ──────────────
^api\.anthropic\.com$
^platform\.claude\.com$
^claude\.ai$
^api\.openai\.com$
^auth\.openai\.com$
^chatgpt\.com$
^api\.scaleway\.ai$
^bedrock-runtime\.eu-west-1\.amazonaws\.com$
^sts\.eu-west-1\.amazonaws\.com$

# ── source code and packages (git push from shell, pack installs) ────────
^github\.com$
^api\.github\.com$
^codeload\.github\.com$
^raw\.githubusercontent\.com$
^objects\.githubusercontent\.com$
^registry\.npmjs\.org$
^pypi\.org$
^files\.pythonhosted\.org$

# ── Claude Code housekeeping (docs lookup, plugin metadata, updates) ─────
^code\.claude\.com$
^downloads\.claude\.ai$
^storage\.googleapis\.com$

# NOT here on purpose:
#   http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com, browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com
#     optional operational telemetry, disabled at the source with
#     CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1
#   googleapis.com (Drive/Docs/Calendar), api.telegram.org, SMTP/IMAP hosts
#     these belong to the GATEWAY, which keeps direct egress: an agent must
#     reach them through a mediated verb, never on its own

# ── added after the first real traffic hit the proxy (see #104) ──────────────
# Bedrock CONTROL plane, distinct from bedrock-runtime: the CLI calls it to
# resolve inference profiles. Missing it broke every SEAL-2 topic, because
# aws-region-eu is the only connected provider with SEAL >= 2.
^bedrock\.eu-west-1\.amazonaws\.com$
# OpenCode model metadata (agents on the opencode runtime: scaleway).
^models\.dev$
# GitHub release assets (downloads referenced by releases).
^release-assets\.githubusercontent\.com$
# The RAG service runs on the HOST and containers reach it by LAN IP. With an
# internal network there is no direct route, so it has to come through here.
# An IP, not a name: the filter matches the CONNECT host verbatim.
^192\.168\.1\.45$
